# DonorLink UG: Phase 2 (Drives, Slots, and Public Drives Pages) Walkthrough

This walkthrough documents the architecture, business rules, query efficiency benchmarks, and verification procedures for **Phase 2: Drives, Slots and the Public Drives Pages** for **Uganda Blood Transfusion Services (UBTS)**.

---

## 1. Architecture & Data Flow

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Staff as UBTS Staff / Admin
    actor Guest as Public Guest / Donor
    participant Web as Web Routes
    participant DriveSvc as DriveService
    participant SlotSvc as SlotService
    participant Gen as SlotGenerator
    participant DB as SQLite DB (UTC storage)
    participant UI as Blade Views (EAT display)

    Note over Staff,UI: Staff Creates and Populates Drive
    Staff->>Web: POST /staff/drives (title, venue, starts_on, ends_on)
    Web->>DriveSvc: create(data, user) (enforces starts_on >= today in EAT)
    DriveSvc->>DB: Stores Drive (status='draft')
    
    Staff->>Web: POST /staff/drives/{id}/slots/generate (dates, times, break, cap)
    Web->>Gen: generate(drive, options) (transactional, skips collisions & breaks)
    Gen->>DB: DB::transaction: bulk inserts Slots (EAT -> UTC conversion)
    
    Staff->>Web: POST /staff/drives/{id}/publish
    Web->>DriveSvc: publish(drive) (requires >= 1 upcoming slot, venue, dates)
    DriveSvc->>DB: Updates status='published'

    Note over Guest,UI: Public Browses Drives
    Guest->>Web: GET /drives
    Web->>DB: Query published & upcoming drives with withSum subqueries (2 queries flat)
    DB-->>UI: Aggregated spots left (capacity - booked_count)
    UI-->>Guest: Renders drive cards with "X spots left" / "Fully booked" (Read-Only)

    Guest->>Web: GET /drives/{id}
    Web->>DB: Fetches drive and upcoming slots (past slots hidden)
    UI-->>Guest: Displays slots grouped by day in EAT (Read-Only, NO booking controls)
```

